Revision: b19f187e9cbe37b5afb1103d88b663253e1f0a03
The port excludes the standalone launchers, compiler selection, upstream memory
monitor, and upstream tests. Compiler API changes target the selected nightly.
The global analysis uses the PAG builder, RCEUS strategy at context depth zero,
call graph, delta propagator, and points-to sets. Stack filtering and cast
pruning are disabled. Complete call bindings remain separate from graph edges.
Generated instance identities and compiler ABI checks are retained.
Backend coverage gaps remain explicit.

The IRQ solver uses demand-driven MIR queries to refine call bindings. It does
not feed facts back into Rupta. The former storage adapter, context cache, and
flow snapshots have been removed. Windows process limits and bounded query
budgets reject incomplete work.

